# Remove Local Authentication in DCORI-Dollarama

Dollarama requires the complete removal of local user authentication within DCORI to enhance the security and integrity of its access control systems. By eliminating local login options, password reset functionalities, and local user management, the organization aims to centralize all authentication processes through Microsoft SSO. This approach mitigates the risks associated with maintaining separate local credentials, such as potential password reuse, weak password policies, and unauthorized access due to overlooked local accounts.

Transitioning exclusively to Microsoft SSO ensures that only users authenticated through Active Directory can access DCORI, aligning with Dollarama’s corporate security standards and compliance requirements. This change not only streamlines user management but also provides a unified and auditable access control mechanism, reducing administrative overhead and improving the organization’s overall security posture.

